---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
---
<figure class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface bin-sequence" aria-labelledby="bin-sequence-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Sequence · A rule across two rows</span>
  <h3 id="bin-sequence-title">Both buyers count the same two mugs</h3>
  <p>At least one mug must remain across the two bins. Each request sells one mug from a different bin, using an ordinary read to check the total first.</p>
  <p class="bin-state"><strong>Before:</strong> left bin 1 + right bin 1 = 2 mugs</p>
  <table>
    <caption>Both reads happen before either write</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Step</th><th scope="col">Request A</th><th scope="col">Request B</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">1</th><td>Reads left 1, right 1.<br />Total 2: decides it can sell one.</td><td>Has not read yet.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">2</th><td>Has not written yet.</td><td>Reads left 1, right 1.<br />Total 2: decides it can sell one.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">3</th><td>Locks and changes the left bin: <strong>1 → 0</strong>.</td><td>Locks and changes the right bin: <strong>1 → 0</strong>.</td></tr>
      <tr><th scope="row">4</th><td>Commits its sale.</td><td>Commits its sale.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="bin-state bin-end"><strong>After:</strong> left bin 0 + right bin 0 = 0 mugs</p>
  <figcaption>Neither bin goes negative. The writes lock different rows, so neither request waits for the other’s decision. The rule about their combined total is broken.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  table { table-layout:fixed; }
  th:first-child { width:2.3rem; }
  caption { text-align:left; color:var(--color-text-secondary); margin:.8rem 0 .3rem; font-size:.8125rem; }
  .bin-state { padding:.6rem 0 .6rem .8rem; border-left:2px solid var(--teal); }
  .bin-end { border-color:var(--gold); }
</style>
